      "content": "From a modern stakeholder perspective, pure neutrality is increasingly difficult to sustain when a major environmental issue is at stake. While silence avoids immediate conflict, it hands the narrative entirely to critics, allowing negative perceptions to solidify as facts. Therefore, while neutrality is *a* option, it is a high-risk defensive maneuver rather than a proactive strategy. A carefully worded, balanced statement that emphasizes your commitment to adapting, even if you don't fully endorse the mandate, is often the strategically safer route.",
